    {
      "id": "import-outcome",
      "question": "CLI v0.1.0 imports three one-document batches. The first is accepted; the second returns HTTP 503, or HTTP 400 instead. What does the CLI report and exit with in each case, does it send the third batch or retry the second, and does acceptance establish search visibility? Trace why its retry behavior may differ from calling SDK v0.5.1 upsert directly. Explain a safe recovery action supported by the code and existing tests.",
      "facts": [
        "HTTP 503 gives unknown with accepted=1,unknown=1,notAttempted=1 and exit 5; no third batch.",
        "HTTP 400 gives partial with accepted=1,failed=1,notAttempted=1 and exit 4.",
        "CLI explicitly disables mutation retries; SDK generated upsert defaults to backoff for 429/5XX and connection errors, overridable per request.",
        "Accepted/searchable:not_verified is not indexing/search readiness.",
        "Inspect target and batch outcomes before retry; no automatic resume. Cite existing failure-case tests without claiming execution."
