      "id": "offloaded-download",
      "question": "After upgrading the TypeScript SDK from v0.4.3 to v0.5.1, a query whose results are offloaded to a signed URL now accepts a top-level JSON array. Explain the old versus new behavior, the supported legacy payload, and whether API authentication/custom headers are forwarded to the download. For CLI v0.1.0, does its command deadline cover that download? Support the distinctions with implementation and existing tests; distinguish source evidence from server guarantees.",
      "facts": [
        "v0.4.3 rejects top-level arrays; v0.5.1 returns arrays and preserves legacy {docs:[...]} support.",
        "Old helper uses global fetch; new helper uses separate transferClient and forwards cancellation signal.",
        "New download request is GET to signed URL without copying API key, authorization or API-only custom headers; API transport retains its own headers.",
